{"id": "EUVD-2026-108851", "enisaUuid": "3c6ee140-b381-3032-8054-806055a8620d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstrparser: make sure __strp_recv isn't running before tearing down the parser\n\nThe comment above strp_done() claims that if strp is stopped,\nstrp_recv will no longer be called. That's only true if the caller has\na mechanism (eg locking) to guarantee that strp_recv() calls that\nstarted before strp_stop() have completed by the time we call\nstrp_done().\n\nThis adds a dummy lock_sock/release_sock pair to guarantee that any\nin-flight strp_recv() (which runs under either bh_lock_sock or\nlock_sock, depending if it's called from ->sk_data_ready or strp_work)\nhas completed.\n\nOnly espintcp can be affected by this race condition, but this patch\nmakes sure no future user of strp can have the bug.\n\nThis could crash on strp->sk (\"general mode\" of strp), but this mode\nhas been here for 9 years and has never been used. It'll be gone soon,\nno point worrying about it.\n\nSwitch the stopped/paused/etc bits to u8's to avoid races between\nstrp_stop() and strp_pause/unpause().\n\nA reproducer has been published and turns the possible UAF into an\nexploit [1].", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a18dd388045dc7263d99a07db9de4e0f149ca8f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f3e9fe1b155e9b4572054d8d140586bc3512ecf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2b5f637b9b67a79a50d42614d10653c13b4e449", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eaa3a29004c063d7e9d5ea55636f693f67e6db0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0984ebc631792acf8fff105112ee74a6b8f1efcc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99056"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02590de0-d695-352f-a32f-d11f5b20b251", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "095e21a1-ea84-3e17-924f-87330467e8ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "48f1036f-cfb2-32ae-9a85-a97050344529", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4fe3077c-ec89-379c-b396-b8acb898fe22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8add68d5-70ef-3a1a-b9ff-7d4ecdd35798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "9fbc142b-3486-382b-bb72-373804d8e49b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "a6d704d9-f8a9-31b8-9216-ced71bc24942", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <9f3e9fe1b155e9b4572054d8d140586bc3512ecf"}, {"id": "a7f7f937-4206-3080-ab1c-dfaa0951c43d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <0984ebc631792acf8fff105112ee74a6b8f1efcc"}, {"id": "b6d9edb6-cdcc-3cee-a517-66ebb160565d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "bd0c825c-ddfd-38a7-96a4-23f61ae970c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <a18dd388045dc7263d99a07db9de4e0f149ca8f1"}, {"id": "de5c4fe6-2250-3877-ba10-cf461735e2cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <eaa3a29004c063d7e9d5ea55636f693f67e6db0f"}, {"id": "f6598962-8ead-337b-a2a1-86e0a65c2d41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27cca96cd68fa2c6814c90f9a1cfd36bb68c593 <d2b5f637b9b67a79a50d42614d10653c13b4e449"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "27842333-7ba4-3eb5-92fb-3dbf5a93057a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}